{"title":"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_[braindead_simple_+_asy_diagram]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 [braindead simple + asy diagram]</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250c18a8571fa03a288a46b620018fe6386120de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d617a9682728d1be7878641ba5681184cd0b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 24,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> and right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792daa030c96693198f143f9176bf888b7ca25cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C.$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d3431b737f3671c3c1d717f039984ff101e97404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on the same side of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4dcfdcb6c55dc976f80f3642376f6b57fbb02a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = BD = 15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"129\" height=\"13\" /> Given that the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15ef54a96b558f4dc28307ddc3e86cb48d81a978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDM$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> may be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d79212320059df1578b25455206c82c61282fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {m\\sqrt {n}}{p},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"50\" height=\"42\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed17364b06ad42c2450df4d0f6a0f06034086bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/2713658021a15e0d7dc624a50e14497d5841b406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n + p.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to determine that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0e663a84db794612f276a19bd914ace4165a6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=25.$\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the orthogonal projection from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecee609050b0744995a1b79ec0fcd162a97441b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541063e059abdea85f39497c2fb1a73ba3244d9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CDM]=\\frac{(DM)(MN)} {2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/0380c4e2a4915f5b6e23eaab58358216fbb00c1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN=BN-BM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/2564c9ce1bddb69a95dc00a352d58b37c0830bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=\\frac{24 \\cdot 7} {2} =\\frac{25 \\cdot (CN)} {2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"229\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>From the third equation, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2db34e80aa86409aee90faa9c71c4f8e4ded1436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CN=\\frac{168} {25}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19cafb60555f7f7becf394f468fc8788aad6923c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta BCN,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185f2e02bb3d55b30ae5eecf0663e7fa8d2f4773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BN=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{24 \\cdot 25} {25}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{24 \\cdot 7} {25}\\right)^2}=\\frac{24} {25}\\sqrt{25^2-7^2}=\\frac{576} {25}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"449\" height=\"56\" /> \n</p><p>Thus, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/7672b961ebbd73925471ae403f0fa77c5569b1e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN=\\frac{576} {25}-\\frac{25} {2}=\\frac{527} {50}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a199efc419bb1d1675df242c9aab901e64eb7bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ADM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, we use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> to get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1fb10a49f9453b3025abbb728fd2684718a65f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM=\\sqrt{15^2-\\left(\\frac{25} {2}\\right)^2}=\\frac{5} {2} \\sqrt{11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"255\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Thus, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd47da2522716038ca244ba8cb09350b41a50b59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CDM]=\\frac{527 \\cdot 5\\sqrt{11}} {50 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2}= \\frac{527\\sqrt{11}} {40}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"263\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0dcd003bd7927af902779eecc820b93bcca074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$527+11+40=\\boxed{578}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"178\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ minor edits by kundusne000\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a79261daa583cc78a1b13a23ac574de93d7a86df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AMD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fc0ad463cb70a65668f411d165e87530a7fc6c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM=\\frac{5\\sqrt{11}} {2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"41\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumcenter and thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb80be13bf764f11f7db54a66fe53c13f6526ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM=\\frac{25} {2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" />. We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a593938d8f2efbdb446bc9a93207fb297f6d38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CMD=\\theta$\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5ab17bd49d151d4f5f7e71b781d118c7f957555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24^2 = 2 \\cdot (12.5)^2-2 \\cdot (12.5)^2 * \\cos (90+\\theta).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"333\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda53cb858ac93b658aa6e35af86c20cd0ecd8ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\frac{527} {625}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />. Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3edf5d9c1a57bca3d53ca31ce2f1c39838be8ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CMD]=\\frac{1} {2} (12.5) \\left(\\frac{5\\sqrt{11}} {2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{527} {625}\\right)=\\frac{527\\sqrt{11}} {40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"368\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is plotted on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_plane\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cartesian plane\">cartesian plane</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e6208c2cb42a23c2262f44fcfc5e8f218cb2d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f660fb19ba1d6b58ebb5e675b4f3456f8d4f67c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(24,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />.\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c87a45101f9eee3c9a9f44c5c9041723c3c43b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12,3.5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5124d12a805a9f977f2ffa46dc710c4a39ed35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABD$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f00f55b6b1cf59b8a3b3687a2b9aed8b37578c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b636b1a91744e4aa634c1f5aa65f4fe1007be88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=12.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164068ebb933b8e3137c747adbeae033726a41ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=15, MD=2.5\\sqrt{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />.\nThe slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d91857f8397f440572dd05303280443a69e6c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{7}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"37\" /> so the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f00f55b6b1cf59b8a3b3687a2b9aed8b37578c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a6e4acca80a643b3e0b42362234459314ecc441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{24}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\nDraw a vertical line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and a horizontal line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose these two lines meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e66fe64bf7e996a7c04431d657c432b0ab08487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MX=\\frac{24}{7}DX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/eadca2dd93bbbde68b0492b8559235cf920349fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD=\\frac{25}{7}DX=\\frac{25}{24}MD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"194\" height=\"38\" /> by the pythagorean theorem.\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94a5cb590f96b28b345959a770f8857d3e36bbcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MX=2.4\\sqrt{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9ebe54133f3225ab3d5eed5670bc6f87aa217692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DX=.7\\sqrt{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> so the coordinates of D are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ce5aed81470bdf62ec165609cccd020c70b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12-.7\\sqrt{11},\\, 3.5-2.4\\sqrt{11})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"24\" />.\nSince we know the coordinates of each of the vertices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0afabb1720b3a3cb8be7f5d869428904a00e7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CMD$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" />, we can apply the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a> to find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aad5799f8874e933beed35ae99c9f277088d28d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CMD, \\frac{527 \\sqrt{11}}{40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>~ minor edit by kundusne000\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5d96c8d1e481244e028c9e97d1d7b53206536b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />.  Since triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881d0f5a82e841846355420f3e52141021c5a5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CME$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0afabb1720b3a3cb8be7f5d869428904a00e7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CMD$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> share a side and height, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b325adae48558d10f5cedf4740f610a5d1e970c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CDM$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c33438fea8461d9b58b359ced6e204549704cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DM}{EM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"37\" /> times the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881d0f5a82e841846355420f3e52141021c5a5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CME$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />.\nBy AA similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e30d66cbd8b17f232a97b595186fa62668338c91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta EMB$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fd024495151f05d094213ff2042102027e1e5a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ACB$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be50115573a00da5ca7efb15c88bc3faa536d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{EM}{AC}=\\frac{MB}{CB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"99\" height=\"37\" />. Solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cdaebe44cbf3fb847b1bd11ceb998efff9bbe1ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EM=\\frac{175}{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />. Using the same method but for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bbe91133fdaa92f3e58b137fdb4db178296da61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14f3188dc48c7ff673af519a79610871f3ad1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB=\\frac{625}{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />. As in previous solutions, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c7e862df6db5ae7cd8b469e1149fbe247a8b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM=\\frac{5\\sqrt{11}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"41\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8be9c178ae5e684557328be9916b1a03100130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DM}{EM}=\\frac{24\\sqrt{11}}{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"41\" />.\nNow, since we know both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bbe91133fdaa92f3e58b137fdb4db178296da61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d7c4c331dcdc44b3b29b06ecd29fe56bdad4f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=\\frac{527}{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />. The height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881d0f5a82e841846355420f3e52141021c5a5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CME$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> is the length from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, the height is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41d70da69fcc67b8c7648ce118df81757be8b52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot7=\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" />. Using this, we can find that the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0afabb1720b3a3cb8be7f5d869428904a00e7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CMD$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93affe2cfae097a19f21f5183b65f4402624e60e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot\\frac{527}{48}\\cdot\\frac{24\\sqrt{11}}{35}=\\frac{527\\sqrt{11}}{40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"239\" height=\"41\" />, giving our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296bf646a7c036ec6bacdd354d44acd225e59511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{578}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by someonenumber011.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.5Bbraindead_simple_.2B_asy_diagram.5D\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_[braindead_simple_+_asy_diagram]\">Solution 5 [braindead simple + asy diagram]</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 [braindead simple + asy diagram]\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d50a58c91ccf62d752f1eb080e2fc06a86d98e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; unitsize(0.25cm); pair A = (0,0); pair B = (7,24); pair C = (7,0); dot(&quot;A&quot;,A,SW); dot(&quot;B&quot;,B,NE); dot(&quot;C&quot;,C,SE); draw(A--B--C--cycle); pair M = (7/2,12); pair D = (11.459,9.678); dot(&quot;M&quot;,M,NW); dot(&quot;D&quot;,D,NE); draw(A--D); draw(C--M--D--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"178\" height=\"325\" />\nFirst, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d99d79bf951748fcae70ae8df60694b7e462918.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BM = AM = \\frac{25}{2}.\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"38\" /> Further, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/7/0672874eb237605c142c54c52b87e9c56cecfd42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC] = \\frac{7*24}{2}=84. \\frac{[\\triangle{AMC}]}{\\triangle{ABC}}=\\frac{AM}{AB}=\\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386faa1d8f776c59ea3d0fc37906909c0f02d2e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\therefore [\\triangle{AMC}]=42\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />\nThen, also notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d0574d6575830f872dec5fc4de757f23cea84426.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[AMDC] =[\\triangle{AMD}]+[\\triangle{ACD}]=[\\triangle{AMC}]+[\\triangle{CMD}]=42+[\\triangle{CMD}]\\]\" width=\"572\" height=\"18\" />\nSo we can say:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29f9ca61f3bd73ea1733158042610c4ec6f1dbb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle{CMD}]=[\\triangle{AMD}]+[\\triangle{ACD}]-42\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"18\" />\nThen, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2d753a273fa7407971ff430d535086528dc49be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle{AMD}] = AM * MD /2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"20\" /> since D lies on the perpindicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692843d72b673ee70bf2a2ea1c48be069d0a7dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=BD=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" />) and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b983c84429df316eb5c87454f166f9f34db1292.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AM} \\perp \\overline{MD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/d/dadb8f693c2408893ac0b2ae53aaf4a4c5303e4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[MD  = \\sqrt{15^2-\\frac{25^2}{4}}= \\frac{5\\sqrt{11}}{2}\\implies [\\triangle{AMD}]=\\frac{25}{2}*\\frac{5\\sqrt{11}}{2}*\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{125\\sqrt{11}}{8}\\]\" width=\"560\" height=\"43\" />\nNow, take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc569f28fce91750c5ede8db1251464d4a92cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\angle{CAB},\\beta = \\angle{DAM},\\gamma = \\beta-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"286\" height=\"18\" />. Then, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a01c47a39be536c3dd7b68d3c7df41569e1fbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\beta) = \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6},\\cos(\\beta) =\\frac{5}{6},\\sin(\\alpha) =24/25,\\cos(\\alpha)=7/25\\]\" width=\"447\" height=\"41\" />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72731ce8fea645dfb3e4fefcf64df8bfa1de8ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\gamma)=\\sin(\\alpha-\\beta)=\\frac{24}{25}*\\frac{5}{6} - \\frac{7}{25}*\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}=\\frac{120-7\\sqrt{11}}{150}\\]\" width=\"446\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9d4b83d5048b23a84c8bd78f45c310bef0572a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle{ACD}]=\\frac{7*15*\\sin(\\gamma)}{2}=\\frac{7}{2}*\\frac{120-7\\sqrt{11}}{10}=42-\\frac{49\\sqrt{11}}{20}\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"41\" />\nand thus:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/04854619ac7a9f9643d7c44c5b9137737db38306.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle{CMD}]=42-\\frac{49\\sqrt{11}}{20}+\\frac{125\\sqrt{11}}{8}-42=\\frac{625\\sqrt{11}-98\\sqrt{11}}{40}=\\frac{527\\sqrt{11}}{40}\\implies m+n+p = 527+11+40=\\boxed{\\textbf{578}}\\]\" width=\"842\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Video Solution from Khan Academy: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=smtrrefmC40\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=smtrrefmC40</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II\" title=\"2003 AIME II\">2003 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201247\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.059 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.078 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 678/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21850/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.717      1 -total\n 58.48%    7.437      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.04%    4.965      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3103:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201247 and revision id 289631. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}